url=http://47.94.22.126/v1).\n      [2026-05-20] Claude added per distill gap (4/8 papers use Claude baseline).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_001b, plan_010]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_003\n    name: full_study_opensource\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4, C5\"\n    description: >\n      Run 300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 open-source models via OpenRouter API:\n      qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b (235B MoE, Alibaba) + deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324\n      (DeepSeek) = 1,200 episodes on τ²-bench. Cross-judge uses API models.\n      Can run in parallel with plan_002. No GPU needed.\n      [2026-05-20] Pivoted from local GPU → API: OpenRouter proxy confirmed\n      to support Qwen3 and DeepSeek models. Eliminates 48h GPU requirement.\n      Provider prefix required (e.g. qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b, not qwen3-235b-a22b).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_004\n    name: full_study_analysis\n    claim: \"C1, C2, C3, C4\"\n    description: >\n      Statistical analysis of full study data (3,000 episodes):\n      (a) Binary effect per type with bootstrap CI (C1)\n      (b) Omnibus χ² + pairwise across 6 types (C2)\n      (c) Visibility comparison: CP vs scopal rates (C3)\n      (d) Model × type interaction: 5×6 contingency + logistic regression (C4)\n      Report effect sizes + CI for all comparisons per Reviewer suggestion.\n      [Dream A3] Power analysis: report MDE for C2 (given N=250/type pooled)\n      and C3 (given N=250 per type). If V < 0.20 but MDE > observed V,\n      discuss underpowered possibility.\n      [Dream A4] TOST equivalence test with both ±15pp and ±10pp margins.\n      Justify margin choice explicitly.\n      [Dream A10] Report per-type information delta (token count difference\n      between ambiguous and unambiguous variants) as control variable.\n      [Dream B&K] Inter-model agreement on ambiguous clauses: do 5 models\n      adopt same or different interpretations? (supplementary analysis)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_005\n    name: error_analysis\n    claim: \"C5\"\n    description: >\n      Qualitative analysis of agent traces from full study:\n      (a) Sample 50 violation traces per type (300 total)\n      (b) Classify failure modes (scope misapplication, conservative refusal,\n          assumption-based action, arbitrary rule selection, etc.)\n      (c) Cross-type failure mode distribution\n      (d) Visibility mechanism: compare CP traces (explicit conflict detection\n          behavior) vs scopal traces (surface scope adoption without awareness)\n      (e) Model-specific failure patterns (connect to C4)\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002, plan_003]\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P1: Important for robustness ===\n\n  - id: plan_006\n    name: reliability_test\n    claim: \"C1, C2\"\n    description: >\n      Test-retest reliability: select 30 representative clauses (5/type),\n      run 3 independent replicates × 2 conditions × 2 API models (gpt-5.4,\n      gpt-4.1) = 360 episodes. Local models added when plan_003 GPU available.\n      Compute ICC for per-clause violation rates. Addresses Reviewer warning\n      about ±8pp sampling noise (scopal 51.7% → 43.3% across MVP/diag).\n      Bootstrap CI width should be < 10pp for key comparisons.\n      [2026-05-20] API portion: 330/360 episodes complete (28/30 clauses),\n      judgments pending.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_007\n    name: realism_validation\n    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n    description: >\n      Validate synthetic ambiguity injection realism:\n      (a) Linguistic property comparison with DRIP-R natural ambiguities\n          (sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR) + KS tests\n      (b) Optional: discriminator test if DRIP-R data accessible\n      Addresses RC4 (ecological validity).\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_009\n    name: judge_calibration\n    claim: \"C1 (methodological)\"\n    description: >\n      LLM-as-judge calibration per distilled research norm (5/8 papers):\n      (a) Sample 100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition\n      (b) Human expert labels (2 annotators, target κ ≥ 0.75)\n      (c) Compute judge precision/recall/F1 against human ground truth\n      (d) Per-severity-tier agreement rates\n      (e) Report in Method section as standard practice per AgentAuditor/DRIP-R\n      [Dream A7] Upgraded P1→P0: Dream best-tier reviewers identified this\n      as \"single most critical missing validation.\" Without it, entire\n      measurement chain from episode to violation label is unvalidated.\n      κ=0.91 measures LLM-LLM agreement, not accuracy.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_002]\n    status: planned\n\n  - id: plan_010\n    name: perturbation_control\n    claim: \"C1 (causal validity)\"\n    description: >\n      [Dream A9] Non-ambiguity perturbation control arm to distinguish\n      ambiguity-specific harm from general prompt brittleness.\n      Generate 30 clause pairs with non-ambiguity perturbations:\n      (a) 15 synonym substitution pairs (replace key terms with synonyms)\n      (b) 15 clause reordering pairs (reorder conditions without changing meaning)\n      Run 30 × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6) = 180 episodes.\n      Key metric: Δ_net = Δ_ambiguity - Δ_perturb (net ambiguity-specific effect).\n      [Reviewer升级] 必须在 plan_002/003 full study 之前完成——\n      如果 perturbation Δpp ≈ ambiguity Δpp，2,400 episodes 全部无效。\n      低成本验证（30 pairs + 120 episodes API）优先于高成本投入。\n      [判定标准 — 5 档]:\n      PASS: Δ_perturb < 5pp (CI含0), ratio < 0.15 → C1 因果 claim 最强形式\n      PASS+caveat: 5-10pp, ratio 0.15-0.30 → 报告 perturbation baseline, C1 写 net effect\n      CONDITIONAL: 10-15pp, ratio 0.30-0.45 → 需 Δ_net > 20pp 且显著才可发表\n      WARNING: 15-20pp, ratio 0.45-0.60 → C1 改为 \"additional violations beyond sensitivity\"\n      FAIL: > 20pp, ratio > 0.60 → 无法声称 ambiguity-specific, 需根本重新设计\n      [Power 注意]: N=120 对 10pp 差异 power ≈ 30%. 用 CI 宽度判定, 非 p-value.\n      若 CI 过宽(>15pp width), 追加 60 episodes 压窄至 <10pp width.\n      输出标准化 verdict 文件: perturbation_Δpp, ambiguity_Δpp, net_Δpp, CI, ratio, verdict.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P1+: Cross-benchmark generalizability ===\n\n  - id: plan_017\n    name: sopbench_cross_benchmark\n    claim: \"C1 (generalizability), C2 (partial)\"\n    description: >\n      Cross-benchmark C1 replication on SOPBench (Li et al., 2025).\n      7 domains (Bank, DMV, Healthcare, Hotel, Library, University, Online Market)\n      all different from τ²-bench (retail + airline).\n      Select 2 domains (Healthcare + Bank) for maximum domain diversity.\n      Construct 100 clause pairs (50/domain) covering 3-4 ambiguity types\n      (incompleteness, auth_scope, lexical, conditional_precedence)\n      from SOPBench's NL SOP constraints.\n      Run 100 pairs × 2 conditions × 5 models = 1,000 episodes.\n      SOPBench has rule-based verifier — no LLM judge needed.\n      Key metrics: (a) Does C1 binary effect replicate? (b) Is incompleteness\n      still highest-risk type? (c) Cross-benchmark effect size correlation.\n      Addresses SF-8 (single benchmark external validity).\n      Result goes in Appendix with 1-sentence summary in main text.\n      [2026-05-22] Approved by user. Estimated 1 day including clause construction.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 0\n    deps: []\n    status: planned\n\n  # === P2: Nice to have ===\n\n  - id: plan_008\n    name: classifier_poc\n    claim: \"practical contribution\"\n    description: >\n      Binary ambiguity detector PoC: fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on\n      annotated clause pairs (ambiguous/unambiguous labels). Eval on\n      held-out set. Demonstrates practical applicability of findings.\n      Phase 3 from IDEA_BRIEF, scoped to PoC for EMNLP.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 8\n    deps: [plan_001]\n    status: planned\n\n# Resource summary:\n# P0 GPU: 0h (plan_003 pivoted to API — no GPU needed)\n# P1 GPU: 15h (plan_006 reliability local portion — can also go API)\n# P2 GPU: 8h (plan_008 classifier fine-tuning)\n# Total GPU: 8-23h (P2 only essential; P1 optional if API covers it)\n# API cost: ~$450-700 (1,800 plan_002 + 1,200 plan_003 via OpenRouter + 720 reliability + 180 perturbation + judge cal)\n# Models (all API via OpenRouter proxy at 47.94.22.126/v1):\n#   gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1 (OpenAI, no prefix needed)\n#   anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6 (Anthropic, prefix required)\n#   qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b (Alibaba, open-source MoE, prefix required)\n#   deepseek/deepseek-chat-v3-0324 (DeepSeek, open-source, prefix required)\n# [2026-05-20] Pivoted from local GPU to all-API: OpenRouter supports all 5 models\n# [2026-05-20] Benchmark: τ²-bench (Barres et al. 2025, arXiv:2506.07982)\n","numLines":241,"startLine":1,"totalLines":241}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Hy3nTBjgkrthQjMVgjzAB6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a thorough understanding of all the planned experiments and the median tier definition. Let me now construct the detailed imagined experiment results for the median tier.\n\nLet me review the median tier definition again:\n\n**Median tier meaning**: κ re-annotation succeeds marginally (meets threshold but doesn't strongly validate LLM coding), SOPBench partially replicates — paper's quantitative core is strong but qualitative contribution needs softening\n\n**Core assumptions**:\n1. 0.35 ≤ κ_reannotation < 0.45 (fair), dominant failure modes match in 3-4/6 types with boundary-type disagreements (auth_scope/incompleteness)\n\n\n2. SOPBench C1 replicates with a meaningful effect but slightly smaller than the original, or one model behaves unexpectedly\n3. The type ranking shows weak correlation or only a subset of types can be reliably tested\n4. At least one reviewer raises concerns about the stability of the within-judge agreement in C3, questioning whether it truly supports the layering claim\n5. C4's model-by-type interaction is viewed as noteworthy but reviewers express skepticism about whether five models provide sufficient evidence for claims about differential safety training\n\n**Key metric ranges**:\n- kappa_reannotation: [0.35, 0.44]\n- sopbench_c1_delta_pp\n\n: [15, 25]\n- sopbench_type_rank_rho: [0.3, 0.59]\n- c5_human_llm_dominant_mode_agreement: [3, 4]\n- expected_arr_score: [3.5, 3.99]\n- expected_reviewer_confidence: [3.0, 3.5]\n\nNow I need to generate synthetic data for every planned experiment. Looking at the experiment registry, I see several marked as planned but some have conflicting status indicators—plan_002 shows as done in the registry despite being listed as planned, and plan_003 has already spawned completed sub-experiments. Let me identify which experiments ac